# Mobile app environment overrides — copy to `.env` locally (never commit `.env`).
# All values below are placeholders; no real credential or endpoint belongs here
# (constitution rule 16 — secrets never enter source, examples, or logs).
#
# NOTE: this foundation prompt does not yet wire a config-loading library
# (e.g. react-native-config) to read this file into the app automatically —
# see mobile/src/api/getApiBaseUrl.ts's `apiBaseUrlOverride` seam. Wiring that
# up is a follow-up; until then this file documents the intended variable
# name only.

# Full backend base URL including the /v1 version segment.
# Leave unset for local development against the Android emulator / iOS
# simulator default (see getApiBaseUrl.ts). Required for any release build.
API_BASE_URL=https://api.example.invalid/v1
